A||||7||ChadMan||Beach vacation advice?||||5||
Z||000000||ChadMan||04-09-2001||11:16 AM||||My wife and I are hoping for a quiet week at the beach in late June.  Our only requirements:<P>a)  We'd like to spend less than $1,000 on accommodations for the week<BR>b)  Must be 1,000 miles or less from Columbus, OH - we're driving<BR>c)  The less crowded, the better<P>Any suggestions for places to go?  How's the Outer Banks area?  Thanks in advance...||||reg||5
Z||000001||WampusCat||04-09-2001||11:45 AM||||Corolla, NC is really nice because a state beach with absolutely nothing on it starts on the north end of town and goes to VA.  It's been about 7 years since I was there but it was really nice back then. Cool lighthouse too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Taijiguy||04-09-2001||11:58 AM||||There's a place called Sandbridge, it's about 10 miles south of Virginia Beach. Very isolated. It may cost a wee bit over your budget to stay there, but it's great. It's not crowded, since no one knows about it, but it's close enough that you can go hit the boardwalk in Va Beach if you want. There's also a place in Delaware called Bethany Beach. It's also off the beaten path, about 15 miles south of Ocean City. Again, far enough to be pleasant, but close enough you can still go to enjoy the nightlife.<BR>~Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||04-09-2001||12:16 PM||||Its a bit far, but Gulf-Shores, AL is very nice(about 20 miles West of FL). It has been getting more and more touristy there every year though, and I didn't have the $$$ to make it down this year. There is an awsome state owned hotel right on the beach with a couple miles of private beach. I can't remember exactly how much it is per night there, but when myself and 3 friends went down once, it was just a tad over $400/night. Cut that in half since there is only two of you, should be cheaper. Plus, free food, and all sorts of activities nearby.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FOCONE||04-09-2001||12:32 PM|||| Got you covered....<BR>June 15-16 Fiero Owner's Club of New England<BR>6th annual Fiero show weekend<BR>Old Orchard Beach, Maine<BR>Quite, only 828.6 miles, mid to late June not crowded<BR>and you can bring your Fiero to the show,<BR>make the wife happy (vacation, under 1k)<BR>and come to a fiero show. <BR>You could get here and back, spend a week<BR>for less then a grand. Lots to do<BR>not just the beach.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChadMan:<BR><B>My wife and I are hoping for a quiet week at the beach in late June.  Our only requirements:<P>a)  We'd like to spend less than $1,000 on accommodations for the week<BR>b)  Must be 1,000 miles or less from Columbus, OH - we're driving<BR>c)  The less crowded, the better<P>Any suggestions for places to go?  How's the Outer Banks area?  Thanks in advance...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||7
Z||000005||loafer87gt||04-09-2001||12:55 PM||||I'm not sure how far you want to travel, but Watertown lakes in Alberta is an absolutely beautiful place to visit. It has some of the most breathtaking scenery I have ever seen, and has some of the worlds best hiking trails. It is a vey quiet place to visit, and not nearly as crowded as Banff or Jasper. The tempereratures during the summer are usually around 30 degrees C, and there are a couple of nice small beaches that you can hike to. It is located right in the corner bottom corner between Alberta and BC. THe way our dollar is now, your $1000 dollars would go a long way.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||04-10-2001||11:00 AM||||Thanks for the tips.  Now I have some more destinations to check out...<P>Unfortunately, I can't attend the FOCONE show.  Every vacation my wife and I have taken since getting married has been to visit her mom  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> or to attend Fiero shows, so we agreed to do neither on our vacation this year!||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||04-10-2001||11:58 AM||||I say drive to the airport and get on a plane for Cozumel, Mexico. For my wife and I to go it was only $1100 for both of us including airfare, 5 days, 4 nights including all meals and beverages at the very nice El Cozumeleno resort. Cozumel is home to the second largest coral reef in the world, so if you've ever wanted to go snorkling in warm crystal blue water, that's the spot. Great window shopping and very friendly people. Extremely low crime rate as it's an island (where would criminals hide?) and very good food. ||||reg||1
